.Dd June 27, 2026
.Dt CAPSICUM 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm Capsicum
.Nd lightweight OS capability and sandbox framework
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "options CAPABILITY_MODE"
.Cd "options CAPABILITIES"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a lightweight OS capability and sandbox framework implementing a hybrid
capability system model.
.Nm
is designed to blend capabilities with UNIX.
This approach achieves many of the benefits of least-privilege operation, while
preserving existing UNIX APIs and performance, and presents application authors
with an adoption path for capability-oriented design.
.Pp
Capabilities are unforgeable tokens of authority that can be delegated and must
be presented to perform an action.
.Nm
makes file descriptors into capabilities.
.Pp
.Nm
can be used for application and library compartmentalisation, the
decomposition of larger bodies of software into isolated (sandboxed)
components in order to implement security policies and limit the impact of
software vulnerabilities.
.Pp
.Nm
provides two core kernel primitives:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It capability mode
A process mode, entered by invoking
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
in which access to global OS namespaces (such as the file system and PID
namespaces) is restricted; only explicitly delegated rights, referenced by
memory mappings or file descriptors, may be used.
Once set, the flag is inherited by future children processes, and may not be
cleared.
.Pp
Access to system calls in capability mode is restricted: some system calls
requiring global namespace access are unavailable, while others are
constrained.
The only system call that requires capability mode to invoke is
.Xr pdself 2 ,
which returns a process descriptor for the calling process.
.Pp
Instead of separate capability-mode system call variants,
.Nm
uses the per-descriptor
.Dv UF_CAP_SUFFICIENT
flag to bypass ambient authority checks.
When a capability-mode process operates on a descriptor that has
.Dv UF_CAP_SUFFICIENT
set, MAC policy, DAC credential re-validation, and jail confinement
checks are skipped \(em the descriptor's capability rights are treated
as sufficient authority.
The flag may be set directly on individual descriptors via
.Xr cap_ambient_limit 2 .
.Pp
For instance,
.Xr sysctl 2
can be used to query process-local information such as address space layout,
but also to monitor a system's network connections.
.Xr sysctl 2
is constrained by explicitly marking \(~~60 of over 15000 parameters as
permitted in capability mode; all others are denied.
.Pp
The system calls which require constraints are
.Xr sysctl 2 ,
.Xr shm_open 2
.Pq which is permitted to create anonymous memory objects but not named ones
and the
.Xr openat 2
family of system calls.
The
.Xr openat 2
calls already accept a file descriptor argument as the directory to perform the
.Xr open 2 ,
.Xr rename 2 ,
etc. relative to; in capability mode the
.Xr openat 2
family of system calls are constrained so that they can only operate on
objects “under” the provided file descriptor.
.It capabilities
Limit operations that can be called on file descriptors.
For example, a file descriptor returned by
.Xr open 2
may be refined using
.Xr cap_rights_limit 2
so that only
.Xr read 2
and
.Xr write 2
can be called, but not
.Xr fchmod 2 .
The complete list of the capability rights can be found in the
.Xr rights 4
manual page.
.It transfer state
Control whether a descriptor can be passed to another process via
.Xr sendmsg 2
with
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS .
Using
.Xr cap_xfer_limit 2 ,
a descriptor's transfer state can be set to single-use
.Pq Dv CAP_XFER_ONCE
or fully locked
.Pq Dv CAP_XFER_NONE .
Transfer state is orthogonal to capability rights.
.Pp
.Xr cap_mmap_capmode 2
sets a monotonic per-descriptor flag that requires the calling process
to be in capability mode before the descriptor may be mapped with
.Xr mmap 2 .
This is useful for shared memory descriptors that should only be
accessible to sandboxed processes.
.Pp
.Xr cap_lookup_capmode 2
sets a monotonic per-descriptor flag on a directory descriptor that
requires the calling process to be in capability mode before the
descriptor may be used as the
.Fa dirfd
argument to any
.Xr \&*at 2
system call.
.It Dv LOCAL_CAP_REQ
The
.Dv LOCAL_CAP_REQ
socket option
.Pq set via Xr setsockopt 2 on Dv SOL_LOCAL
requires the calling process to be in capability mode to send or receive
on that socket end.
It is monotonic and cannot be cleared.
This allows per-end control on socketpairs: the supervisor sets
.Dv LOCAL_CAP_REQ
on the child's end before delegating it.
.It connection-level capability enforcement
The
.Dv LOCAL_CAP_CONNECT
.Ux Ns -domain
socket option
.Pq see Xr unix 4
restricts connections to a listening socket so that only processes in
capability mode may connect.
Attempts to
.Xr connect 2
from a process not in capability mode fail with
.Er ENOTCAPABLE .
The option is monotonic and cannot be cleared once set.
.Pp
The complementary
.Dv LOCAL_CAPMODE_SERVER
option is set on the client socket before connecting.
It requires that the listening socket was created by a process in
capability mode.
If the server is not in capability mode,
.Xr connect 2
fails with
.Er ENOTCAPABLE .
Together these options provide mutual attestation between sandboxed
peers.
.El
.Pp
In some cases,
.Nm
requires use of alternatives to traditional POSIX APIs in order to name
objects using capabilities rather than global namespaces:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It process descriptors
File descriptors representing processes, allowing parent processes to manage
child processes without requiring access to the PID namespace; described in
greater detail in
.Xr procdesc 4 .
.It anonymous shared memory
An extension to the POSIX shared memory API to support anonymous swap objects
associated with file descriptors; described in greater detail in
.Xr shm_open 2 .
.El
.Pp
In some cases,
.Nm
limits the valid values of some parameters to traditional APIs in order to
restrict access to global namespaces:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It process IDs
Processes can only act upon their own process ID with syscalls such as
.Xr cpuset_setaffinity 2 .
.El
.Pp
.Fx
provides some additional functionality to support application sandboxing that
is not part of
.Nm
itself:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Xr capsicum_helpers 3
A set of a inline functions which simplify modifying programs to use
.Nm .
.It Xr libcasper 3
A library that provides services for sandboxed applications, such as operating
on files specified on a command line or establishing network connections.
.El
